def pancake_sort(nums):
    n = len(nums)

    def flip(i):
        nums[:i+1] = reversed(nums[:i+1])

    for i in range(n, 0, -1):
        # Find the index of the maximum element in the remaining unsorted part
        max_index = 0
        for j in range(1, i + 1):
            if nums[j] > nums[max_index]:
                max_index = j

        # Flip the subarray containing the current maximum element to its correct position
        flip(max_index)
        flip(i)
```

In this solution, the `pancake_sort` function sorts the given list of integers using the pancake sort algorithm. The `flip` helper function is used to reverse the order of elements from the start up to (but not including) the specified index. The main loop iterates from the end of the list towards the beginning, finding the maximum element in the remaining unsorted part and flipping it to its correct position. This process repeats until all elements are sorted.

